      "id": "s3",
      "description": "For each radiator that passes the aging constraint, run simulations at multiple thickness values (e.g., 2 cm, 3 cm, 4 cm, 5 cm) within the 1-6 cm range to map out the pion/kaon separation performance as a function of thickness."
    },
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "description": "Analyze simulation results to identify which radiator-thickness combinations achieve the minimum 3.5 sigma separation requirement at 10 GeV/c."
    },
    {
      "id": "s5",
      "description": "Among the configurations meeting all hard constraints (≥3.5 sigma separation and <10% transparency loss), select the optimal radiator and thickness that maximizes pion/kaon separation at 10 GeV/c, and record the final recommendation with supporting performance metrics."
    }
  ]
}
